column4:
INPS, in agreement with the Ministry of Labour and Social Policies, the Ministry of Economy and Finance (MEF) and the National Labour Inspectorate (INL), has developed the Statistical Indicators of Contribution Reliability (Indicatori Statistici di Affidabilità Contributiva, known as ISAC) in order to promote preventive contribution compliance and to identify cases of under-declaration of employment, by means of indicators that compare tax and social security contribution data.
The process provides for compliance letters to be sent to companies, setting out any deviations in the indicators, as determined by the Institute.
Once the compliance letters have been sent, companies may justify and explain the deviations, including by attaching appropriate documentation, by submitting specific communications through the INPS channels.
The generative AI component operates in the analysis of the communications submitted by companies: it analyses and assesses the replies and any attachments in line with the deviations determined by the Institute; it extracts the evidence provided by the company; it assigns the companies’ replies to specific clusters; it proposes an explainable justification of the analysis carried out and also prepares a draft reply to the company itself.
INPS staff govern the entire process: they examine, modify, supplement and/or validate the output produced by the AI system, that is, they retain responsibility for the final decision in providing feedback to the company.
The outcomes feed into monitoring, enabling continuous improvement of the system.
The first application concerns the “Wholesale food trade” sector and the “Hotel and non-hotel accommodation facilities” sector, for a total of 35,491 companies analysed and 20,038 compliance letters sent. The solution improves consistency, timeliness and traceability and will be extended to six further production sectors, namely:
-	Bar, ice-cream parlour, pastry shop and confectionery production activities, for a total of 91,048 businesses;
-	Retail sale of medical and orthopaedic goods, for a total of 2,551 businesses;
-	Installation of electrical, plumbing and other building installations, for a total of 113,063 businesses;
-	Bespoke and mass production of clothing, accessories and household linen, and related processing, for a total of 17,543 businesses;
-	Hairdressing services, for a total of 38,794 businesses;
-	“Maintenance and repair of motor vehicles, motorcycles and mopeds”, for a total of 49,035 businesses.
The legal entities affected will total 312,034, while approximately 176,000 letters will be sent.

The proposed solution has been designed with features of flexibility and modularity that also allow it to be extended to further processes, promoting the standardisation of activities and the optimisation of the resources employed.
